# File: tests/features/provider-catalog-login.feature
# Generated from: specs/2-add-the-provider-catalog-with-provider-aware-login-and-logout/requirements.md
Feature: Provider catalog with provider-aware /login and /logout

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Built-in providers are present and none is Anthropic
    Given no user configuration
    When providers are listed
    Then "opencode-go", "cline-pass", "openai-codex" and "xai" are present with a base URL, a login kind and a per-model wire format, and none is Anthropic

  @SCN002
  Scenario: OpenCode Go models are discovered with wire format and metadata
    Given a stored "opencode-go" key and a model list of "glm-5.1", "kimi-k3", "gpt-5.5", "minimax-m2.5" and "claude-haiku-5-5"
    When discovery runs
    Then the catalog lists "opencode-go/glm-5.1", "opencode-go/kimi-k3", "opencode-go/gpt-5.5" and "opencode-go/minimax-m2.5" with their wire formats and supplied metadata, and no "claude-haiku-5-5"

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Cache is used on load and failures keep cached models
    Given a cached model list and providers answering 401, 404, an empty list and a network error
    When the catalog loads and then refreshes
    Then the load makes no network call, and the providers record "unauthenticated", "unavailable", "empty" and "offline" with their cached models marked as cached

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Custom provider and filters apply, and a credential in config is rejected
    Given a config with a custom OpenAI-compatible provider, disabledProviders ["xai"], enabledModels patterns, and an entry holding an API key
    When the catalog loads
    Then the custom provider appears, xAI is hidden, only matching models are listed, and the key entry is rejected pointing to "/login" without echoing the value

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Login picker lists providers and Anthropic passes through
    Given the catalog
    When the user runs "/login" and chooses Anthropic
    Then the picker listed Anthropic and every enabled provider with its status, and Claude Code's built-in login ran through next(e) with nothing read or stored by the mod

  @SCN006
  Scenario: API-key login validates before saving
    Given the user chooses OpenCode Go
    When they enter a key in the masked input
    Then a valid key is saved and "Logged in to OpenCode Go" is shown with models refreshed, and an invalid key saves nothing and shows an error

  @SCN007
  Scenario: OAuth login by paste and token refresh
    Given the user chooses OpenAI Codex
    When they paste the redirect URL shown after signing in
    Then the tokens and expiry are saved, the account email is shown, no port is opened, and an expired token is refreshed and saved before the next request

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Logout lists stored accounts and deletes the chosen one
    Given two stored OpenAI Codex accounts
    When the user runs "/logout"
    Then only providers with credentials are listed, the active account is marked, the chosen credential is deleted, and choosing Anthropic runs the built-in logout through next(e)
